<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX2-QA-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX2-QA-003" ;
  triage:title "No upper bound on Herdr prompt text length; an oversized argv can execve-fail (E2BIG) and trip the shared HerdrSpawnBreaker for all Herdr-routed recipients" ;
  triage:description "validate_prompt_text (crates/atm-herdr/src/lib.rs ~635-640) only rejects empty/whitespace text. rebuild_received_hook_dispatch (crates/atm-core/src/nudge_dispatch.rs ~123-128) falls back to the full message text (up to the 1 MiB cap) when envelope.summary is empty (legacy/migrated rows). On Linux a single argv element over MAX_ARG_STRLEN (128 KiB) fails execve with E2BIG, classified as HerdrError::ServerUnavailable, which trips the shared HerdrSpawnBreaker (BreakerPolicy::Shared) for every Herdr recipient. Reported by rust-service-hardening-agent RSH-001 (important) on PR #1186 QA-1 (head 4f77d2fff). Orchestrator ruling: deferred, because sprint AX.2 D7 explicitly states no additional length bound is imposed beyond the operating system's single-argument limit; the real defect is that an argument-size spawn failure is a scoped per-message error and must not be classified as ServerUnavailable / count toward the shared breaker. Tracked as a separate hardening issue." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RSH" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "deferred" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T06:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AX2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T06:31:07Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AX2-QA-003/ax2-4f77d2fff-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AX2-QA-003/ax2-4f77d2fff-2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AX2-QA-003/ax2-4f77d2fff-3> ;
  triage:deferredNote "Sprint AX.2 D7 explicitly imposes no length bound beyond the OS single-argument limit; the shared-breaker misclassification of E2BIG spawn failures is tracked as a separate hardening issue (see references) for a later sprint." ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

